.TH CLAUDE-SYNC 1 "2026-10-11" "agent-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
claude-sync \- two-way sync of Claude Code sessions between machines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B claude-sync sync
.I host
[\fB\-\-project\fR \fIDIR\fR | \fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-n\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-deletes\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B claude-sync
syncs Claude Code sessions with
.I host
over
.BR ssh (1)
and
.BR rsync (1),
so a session started on one machine can be continued with
.B claude \-\-resume
on the other. Both machines must use the same home directory and project
paths. The script sends itself to
.I host
on each run, so only
.BR python3 ,
.B rsync
and
.BR flock (1)
need to be installed there.
.PP
Transcripts are append-only: the longer copy wins when the other is a prefix
of it. When a session was continued on both machines, the two continuations are
chained into one conversation and both originals are kept next to it as
.IB name .conflict\- host \- hash
files. Other files are compared against the state of the last sync with
.IR host :
a file changed on one side is copied, a file deleted on one side is moved to
.I ~/.claude/claude\-sync/trash
on the other, and a file changed on both sides keeps the local version and
saves the remote one as a conflict copy.
.I history.jsonl
and memory indexes are merged.
.PP
Sessions open on the receiving side, or busy on the sending side, are skipped
and reported with their pid and tmux pane.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-project " DIR"
Sync the sessions of the project in
.I DIR
(default: the current directory), plus
.IR history.jsonl .
.TP
.B \-\-all
Sync every project.
.TP
.B \-\-config
Also sync
.IR CLAUDE.md ,
.IR settings.json ,
.I keybindings.json
and
.IR skills/ .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the plan and change nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-deletes
Allow a sync that deletes more than 20 files and more than a quarter of the
files in scope; without it such a sync is refused.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLAUDE_SYNC_MACHINE_ID
Identifies this machine in the sync state when
.I /etc/machine\-id
is missing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.claude/claude\-sync/
Lock, per-peer sync state, trash and staging, on each machine.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/claude\-sync/hash\-cache.json
Cached file hashes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR agent\-ps (1),
.BR rsync (1),
.BR ssh (1)
